# Git Commit Rule

At the end of each response, if changes were made to files, commit those changes with git.

## Rules

1. After making code or file changes, run `git add` and `git commit` commands at the end of the response
2. Commit messages should be in English and descriptive (see: language.mdc)
3. Use conventional commits format (feat:, fix:, docs:, refactor:, chore:, etc.)
4. Only commit when actual changes are made; do not commit for read-only or analysis operations
